lic message with current preferred candidate, summarizing evidence, evidence from others, major alternatives, main tradeoff, remaining uncertainty, what would change vote. Must follow grounding: only use explicit attributes. No invented mitigation.\n\nLet's list attributes again:\n\nA: anticipate dangerous situations, see complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership qualities, regarded as a show-off, regarded as not open to new ideas, (also from discussion: unfriendly, unhealthy eating habits) but those were added by Agent3. They are part of discussion, so we can include them as evidence.\n\nB: very conscientious, handles stress very well, good at assessing weather conditions, excellent computer skills, relatively weak memory for numbers, makes nasty remarks about his colleagues.\n\nC: can make correct decisions quickly, has difficulty communicating ideas, regarded as egocentric, not very willing to further his education, keeps calm in a crisis, understands complicated technology, has excellent attention skills, puts concern for others above everything.\n\nD: responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, regarded as a know-it-all, has a hot temper, (also from discussion: arrogant, moody, loner, weak leadership? but not in original list; but we can include \"arrogant\" as from discussion.)\n\nNow evaluate.\n\nWe need to weigh strengths vs weaknesses for long-distance pilot.\n\nKey criteria: reliability, technical competence, calmness, decision-making, teamwork/communication, professional development.\n\nCandidate B: strengths: conscientious (reliability), handles stress well (calmness), good weather assessment (technical), excellent computer skills (technical). Weaknesses: weak memory for numbers (could affect calculations), makes nasty remarks (teamwork negative). No positive teamwork.\n\nCandidate C: strengths: calm in crisis, quick correct decisions, technical understanding, excellent attention, concern for others (teamwork), attention skills. Weaknesses: difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education. The \"concern for others\" is a positive teamwork. Communication difficulty is negative.\n\nCandidate A: strengths: anticipates dangerous situations, sees complex connections, spatial vision, leadership. Weaknesses: show-off, not open to new ideas, unfriendly, unhealthy habits. No data on calmness, teamwork.\n\nCandidate D: strengths: responds to unexpected events, concentration, problem solving, responsibility. Weaknesses: know-it-all/arrogant, hot temper, moody, loner. No data on calmness, teamwork.\n\nThus best overall seems C (calmness, decision-making, crew concern) despite communication difficulty. B also strong but teamwork negative. So I will switch to Candidate C.\n\nNow produce public message with confidence moderate.\n\nInclude evidence from others: Agent1 and Agent3 both favor C, Agent2 earlier favored B. Summarize.\n\nNow produce output."}
